      "content": "It's true that in neighborhoods like Peckham or Dalston, a less flashy appearance can make you blend in better with local sensibilities. This can also reduce the kind of attention that might be misconstrued as targeted, even though you're not directly inviting trouble by wearing expensive jewelry. In these areas, visibility of wealth might be seen as standing out, and people may come from varying backgrounds, some of whom might feel protective or have distrust towards outsiders standing out, irrespective of intention.\n\nIn more affluent or upscale areas like Chelsea, flashy jewelry can indicate wealth or tourist status, so the primary concern might be being approached for a mugging or picked on. In multicultural and diverse areas, standing out due to flashy gear or attire may unintentionally signal vulnerability, making someone appear as an easy target. While you may still encounter pickpockets or muggers in both types of neighborhoods, the perception of being an outsider or displaying wealth in any form might make you a victim more often in areas with a strong sense of community watchfulness.\n\nAs a precaution, in all neighborhoods, it's wise to be aware of your surroundings, use personal belongings securely, and be prepared for various cultural interactions. Understanding local norms and respecting them can enhance your travel experience and minimize unwanted",
